1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,152
This is Siddhartha.

2
00:00:02,202 --> 00:00:04,172
2,500 years ago,

3
00:00:04,222 --> 00:00:07,400
he was born a prince in the Himalayan foothills.

4
00:00:07,450 --> 00:00:09,176
His father wanted him to be king,

5
00:00:09,226 --> 00:00:10,674
so he kept him in the palace,

6
00:00:10,724 --> 00:00:13,019
away from anything sad.

7
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:13,967
At 29,

8
00:00:14,017 --> 00:00:15,674
he finally stepped outside.

9
00:00:15,724 --> 00:00:16,951
He saw an old man.

10
00:00:17,001 --> 00:00:17,891
A sick man.

11
00:00:17,941 --> 00:00:19,550
A dead body.

12
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:21,617
CHANNA: This happens to everyone, my prince.

13
00:00:21,667 --> 00:00:23,200
CHANNA: Even you.

14
00:00:23,250 --> 00:00:25,220
That night, he left it all,

15
00:00:25,270 --> 00:00:27,182
even his wife and newborn son,

16
00:00:27,232 --> 00:00:28,703
to find out why we suffer,

17
00:00:28,753 --> 00:00:30,550
and how to stop.

18
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:32,419
For six years he barely ate,

19
00:00:32,469 --> 00:00:34,346
hoping it would bring answers.

20
00:00:34,396 --> 00:00:36,350
It almost killed him.

21
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,729
Then a woman named Sujata brought him rice and milk.

22
00:00:39,779 --> 00:00:41,319
He ate, and realised:

23
00:00:41,369 --> 00:00:44,059
starving wasn't the answer either.

24
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,775
So he sat under a tree at Bodh Gaya,

25
00:00:46,825 --> 00:00:48,550
and made a promise.

26
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:51,243
SIDDHARTHA: I will not get up until I understand.

27
00:00:51,450 --> 00:00:53,536
By sunrise, he understood.

28
00:00:53,586 --> 00:00:55,672
We suffer because we always want more.

29
00:00:55,722 --> 00:00:58,691
Let go of that, and suffering ends.

30
00:00:58,850 --> 00:00:59,775
From that day,

31
00:00:59,825 --> 00:01:01,285
people called him the Buddha:

32
00:01:01,335 --> 00:01:03,165
the one who woke up.
